    "title": "Walmart Is Selling Lockable 'Heavy-Duty' Storage Bins for Only $10 - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Brian Obudho ,\n13 hours ago\nThe Arena Media Brands, LLC and respective content providers may receive compensation for some links to products and services on this website.\nA large storage bin is what you need to free up space in your basement or garage. Whether it’s your seasonal sporting equipment, pet supplies, gardening tools, or toys.\nHide unused items using this Hyper Tough large lockable storage bin that’s going for only $10 right now at Walmart. Its usual price tag is $15, so you are getting a 33% discount just in time for your Fall organizing projects.\nIt’s easy to clean, reusable and can be used both indoors and outdoors depending on your needs.\nWhy Shoppers Love This Storage Container With over 20,000 ratings on Walmart's website, it maintains a sparkling 4.7-star out of 5.0 average rating, and three things that make it stand out are its durable construction, versatile use and stackability.\n“These storage containers are of exceptional quality. I particularly appreciate their stackable design,” one reviewer wrote.\n“Very easy to store. Tops click in place so you don't have to worry about them accidentally opening,” another buyer added.\nHyper Tough Large Heavy-Duty Storage Bin , $10 (Was $15) at Walmart Details to Know Capacity: 27 gallons Size : 30.6 in by 20.6 in by 14.3 in Weight : 6.6 lbs. Material : rigid plastic (polypropylene) that resists peeling, dents, rust and stains Lockable : Yes. The lid features six built-in tie-down holes, allowing it to be locked using zip ties or padlocks. The red snap lid adds a pop of color and provides a more secure closure with its snug fit. The lid is designed for easy stacking and reduces toppling when multiple units are stacked on top of each other, letting you utilize the available space.\nAt only $10, you can now hide the mishmash of camping equipment, Legos, holiday décor, winter jackets and a myriad of other house items that you don’t need right now, but still make them easily accessible when you need them.\nIf you spend over $35 on your order, Walmart will ship it to you for free.\nRelated: Walmart Is Selling 'Well-Made' Clear Storage Bins for Only $7\nRelated: Walmart Is Selling a ‘Sturdy’ $74 Rolling Cooler for $35, and Buyers Find It Extra Roomy\n12",
